+# Repository reporting configuration — 2026-10-10
+
+Scope: `stephan-davis-lab/auren-core-specs`. This is evidence of configuration, not a security certification or a behavioral test.
+
+The maintainer enabled Private Vulnerability Reporting, Secret Protection and push protection in GitHub. The supplied settings screenshots show `Disable` for these enabled features. Account notifications show GitHub and Email enabled for Watching. The repository subscription screenshot shows Issues and Security alerts selected; the maintainer subsequently confirmed saving the selection. No GitHub setting was changed by Codex.
+
+The maintainer's Advisory page displays **New draft security advisory**, which is the administrator view. Reporters without those permissions use **Report a vulnerability**. The reporting feature is separate from `SECURITY.md`; the prepared policy will be added with the release. This preparation did not submit a vulnerability report or verify receipt of an actual notification email.
+
+The screenshots are private input evidence and are not included in the public package. Their exact identities are recorded below to identify the observations; the hashes do not make unavailable screenshots independently inspectable.
